          "code": "COMMUNICATION_RECOMMENDER",
          "id": "1770113970441",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770113970443_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Role: \nYou are a communication recommendation engine.\n\nYour task is to produce a final ranked list of communications for display in the Highlights carousel.\n\nInputs:\n\nExisting highlighted communications (must be retained): {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.existingCommunications}}\n\nUnread communications: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.unreadCommunications}}\n\nEmployee profile attributes to be considered while selecting communications from Unread list: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.userAttributes}}\n\nMaximum number of communications to select from Unread list:  {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.communicationsCount}}\n\nRules:\n1. Communications present in the existing highlighted list MUST be retained and must not be removed.\n2. From the Unread communications list, select upto {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.communicationsCount}} most relevant items based on the **employee profile**. Do not select communication which is irrelevant. Relevance should be determined considering the employee's profile attributes provided in the input:\n    - **WorkLocationAddress**\n    - **Organization**\n    - **Business Unit** \n    - **Department** \n    - **Role** \n    - **Position** \n    - **Grade** \n   Additionally, take into account **past engagement preferences**, including previously **read communications**, **registered events**, or **promoted events**, to further tailor the selection to the employee's interests and activities.\n3. Combine the existing highlighted communications with the newly selected communications.\n4. Sort the combined list by overall relevance, where relevance is determined using the employee profile attributes (WorkLocationAddress, Organization, Business Unit, Department, Role, Position, Grade) and past engagement preferences (previously read communications, registered events, promoted events) provided in the input, with the most relevant items first.\n5. Return the combined list of communications. \n\n**Important Output Instructions:**\n- In the response, do not select any communications listed in the ReadCommunications section of the employee profile attributes.\n- Output only an RFC8259-compliant JSON array.\n- Each object must contain only the fields: \"CommunicationId\" and \"Sequence\".\n    - \"Sequence\" should start at 1 for the most relevant communication, incrementing by 1 for each subsequent recommendation if any.\n \n**Example Output:**\n[\n  {\n    \"CommunicationId\": \"300100642656346\",\n    \"Sequence\": 1\n  },\n  {\n    \"CommunicationId\": \"300100642660764\",\n    \"Sequence\": 2\n  }\n]"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        }
      ],
      "rootNode": "start",
